  <graph edgedefault="undirected">
    <node id="&quot;ISABELLA LOUISA GORDON&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Isabella Louisa Gordon is another historical figure who was married to Robert French Handcock, contributing to the social and cultural landscape of 19th-century Britain."&lt;SEP&gt;"Isabella Louisa Gordon was a British socialite and philanthropist, known for her marriage to Annie Phillips and her contributions to women's education and empowerment."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0125</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ANNIE PHILLIPS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Annie Phillips was a British women's rights activist and suffragette, best known for her marriage to Isabella Louisa Gordon and her involvement in the women's suffrage movement."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0125</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LONDON&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"London is the birthplace and primary residence of Isabella Louisa Gordon, and the location of many of her activities and events."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0125</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MANCHESTER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Manchester is the birthplace of Annie Phillips, highlighting her origins and early life."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0125</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;WOMEN'S SUFFRAGE MOVEMENT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The women's suffrage movement was a significant part of both Isabella Louisa Gordon and Annie Phillips' lives, driving their activism and public roles."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0125</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PRIDE OF BRITAIN AWARD&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Pride of Britain Award is an honor given to Isabella Louisa Gordon and Annie Phillips for their contributions to the LGBTQ+ community."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0125</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ROBERT FRENCH HANDCOCK&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Robert French Handcock is a historical figure whose life is described as complex and fascinating, and he was married to Isabella Louisa Gordon."&lt;SEP&gt;"Robert French Handcock was a respected individual of his time, known for his marriage to Isabella Louisa Gordon and his connections to the Anglo-Irish gentry."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0125</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;UK NATIONAL ARCHIVES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The UK National Archives provided records confirming the marriage of Isabella Louisa Gordon and Robert French Handcock."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0125</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ANGLO-IRISH GENTRY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Anglo-Irish gentry was a social class to which Robert French Handcock belonged, highlighting his social status and connections."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0125</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ARISTOCRACY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The aristocracy was a social class with which Robert French Handcock had strong ties, emphasizing his elevated social standing."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0125</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EMMA TAYLOR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Emma Taylor is a historian who conducted a study on lesbian women in Victorian England and provided insights into the lives of Isabella Louisa Gordon and Annie Phillips."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0125</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;JAMES WILSON&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"James Wilson is a historian at the University of Oxford who commented on the significance of the discovery of Isabella Louisa Gordon and Robert French Handcock's marriage."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0125</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EMMELINE PANKHURST&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Emmeline Pankhurst was a prominent figure in the women's suffrage movement, and Annie Phillips attended rallies and protests alongside her."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0125</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;1898&quot;">
